# Wuanberri — server-side environment variables
#
# This file is a CHECKLIST. Copy each variable name into the Vercel dashboard
# (Project → Settings → Environment Variables) and paste the real value
# there. NEVER commit the real values to this repo.
#
# Vercel path: https://vercel.com/dashboard → pick your project →
#   Settings → Environment Variables → "Add New"
#
# Variables are split by which feature needs them.

# ============================================================
# Stripe (required for the "Start trial" / "Go Pro" buttons)
# ============================================================
#
# Where to get them: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys
#   - STRIPE_SECRET_KEY:  Reveal the "Secret key" (sk_test_... in dev,
#                         sk_live_... in prod). Click "Reveal test key" if
#                         you only see a hint.
#   - STRIPE_PRICE_ID:    The recurring Pro price ID. Create one in
#                         Products → Add product → Recurring → set a
#                         7-day trial under "Pricing rules". The ID looks
#                         like "price_1Nxxx...".
#   - STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET: After deploying, in Stripe dashboard go to
#                            Developers → Webhooks → Add endpoint →
#                            URL: https://YOUR-DOMAIN.vercel.app/api/stripe-webhook
#                            Events: checkout.session.completed,
#                                    customer.subscription.deleted
#                            → "Add endpoint" → click into it →
#                            "Reveal" under "Signing secret" → copy whsec_...
#
# Reminder: the PUBLISHABLE key (pk_test_... / pk_live_...) is NOT a secret.
# It goes in assets/__STRIPE_CONFIG__.js via `node scripts/setup-secrets.mjs`.

STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_PRICE_ID=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ============================================================
# Supabase (required for cross-device account sync)
# ============================================================
#
# Where to get them: Supabase dashboard → your project → Settings → API
#   - SUPABASE_URL:        "Project URL" (https://xxxxx.supabase.co)
#   - SUPABASE_ANON_KEY:   "anon public" key. It's safe to expose — the
#                          real boundary is Row Level Security on your
#                          `profiles` table.
#
# Both values ALSO go in assets/__SUPABASE_CONFIG__.js (manually edit the
# file — the URL and anon key are public, just not great in a script
# because they differ per project).
#
# This file is for documentation only; the browser reads from the
# __SUPABASE_CONFIG__.js stub, not from these env vars. Vercel doesn't
# need them either, since auth runs entirely in the browser.

SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ============================================================
# Google sign-in (only if you turn on the "Continue with Google" button)
# ============================================================
#
# Where to get them: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   1. Create a project (or pick an existing one).
#   2. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen → External → fill name/email.
#   3. Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID → Web application.
#   4. Authorized JavaScript origins: add your Vercel URL
#      (e.g. https://wuanberri.vercel.app) AND http://localhost:8000 for dev.
#   5. Copy the Client ID — that one is PUBLIC and goes in
#      assets/__GOOGLE_CONFIG__.js via setup-secrets.mjs.
#   6. Copy the Client secret — that one IS a secret. Paste it below.
#
# Note: the public Client ID is also fine to put in BOTH places (the
# server var is a backup for future server-side verification).

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
